  "verbalization": "Ancistrolikokine B is implicated in the interaction with HEp-2 cells through a series of molecular pathways, all of which converge on the EDD domain protein, DegV family. This protein serves as a common target for multiple compounds, including 2alpha-Hydroxytirotundin, Fumarprotocetraric Acid, and 6(2H)-Benzofuranone, which are all linked to HEp-2. The evidence suggests that Ancistrolikokine B exerts its biological effect by first targeting the DegV family, which in turn influences HEp-2 through various molecular mechanisms. The high scores across the three paths indicate a consistent and robust relationship, suggesting that Ancistrolikokine B may act through a shared pathway involving the DegV family to modulate HEp-2 cell behavior. The integration of these findings highlights a potential mechanism where Ancistrolikokine B's activity is mediated through the DegV family, ultimately affecting HEp-2 cells.",
